---
import Callout from "~/components/illustration-kit/Callout.astro"
import IllustrationFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/IllustrationFigure.astro"

const tosses = ["T", "H", "H", "H"]
---

<IllustrationFigure
  lead="Why can THH beat HHH when both patterns are equally likely in three tosses?"
>
  <p class="text-base leading-normal">
    The first player picks <strong>HHH</strong>. The second picks <strong>THH</strong>.
    H means heads and T means tails. The fourth toss is shown only to reveal the overlap.
  </p>

  <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-4 gap-2 text-center sm:gap-3">
      {tosses.map((toss, index) => (
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-1">
          <span class="text-sm">Toss {index + 1}</span>
          <span class="flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-2 border-ink text-lg font-bold">
            {toss}
          </span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-4 gap-2 sm:gap-3">
      <div class="col-span-3 border-t-4 border-series-blue pt-2 text-base font-bold">
        THH: wins at toss 3
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-4 gap-2 sm:gap-3">
      <div class="col-span-3 col-start-2 border-t-4 border-series-red pt-2 text-base font-bold">
        HHH: would appear at toss 4
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Callout tone="accent">
    <p class="leading-normal">
      <strong>Why THH wins 7 times in 8:</strong> HHH can win only if the first three tosses
      are HHH, a 1 in 8 chance. Otherwise, the first eventual HHH must follow a tail,
      making THH appear one toss earlier.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <Fragment slot="caption">
    The patterns overlap. Each has a 1 in 8 chance in any fixed group of three tosses,
    but that does not give them equal chances of appearing first.
  </Fragment>
</IllustrationFigure>
